From 0de466fb8ca46ae3621363f81c226ead1bd21415 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marnick Vandecauter <security@marnick.net>
Date: Sun, 24 May 2026 22:28:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] F112 (hygiene): add Linux hardening flags to plain
 cmake builds
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Distros that use dpkg-buildflags / rpm %optflags inject these by
default; this block protects operators who build from a tarball via
plain 'cmake .. && make' (the documented path for source builds).

Flags:
- -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=2 — glibc runtime bounds checks on str*/mem*
- -fstack-protector-strong — canaries on functions with stack arrays
- -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now — read-only relocations + immediate symbol resolution

gr-satellites builds libgnuradio-satellites.so as a shared library,
so -fPIC is appropriate (and is already injected by CMake's
POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE on shared targets). -fPIE is deliberately
NOT added here because it would conflict with the shared-library
link step (the linker refuses to mix PIE-compiled objects into a .so
output: "relocation R_X86_64_PC32 against symbol ... can not be used
when making a shared object; recompile with -fPIC"). ASLR for the
operator's gr_satellites executable comes from the Python interpreter
binary, which the distro builds with -fPIE anyway.

All other flags are no-ops on toolchains that don't recognise them.
Guarded by UNIX AND NOT APPLE because macOS uses a different linker
and FreeBSD needs different RELRO syntax.

Reference: audit finding F112 (gr-satellites v5.9.0 audit, 2026-05-24)
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 07f4a8b..8e055e6 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -71,6 +71,26 @@ if((CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "Clang" OR
     add_definitions(-fvisibility=hidden)
 endif()

+########################################################################
+# Hardening flags (Linux/BSD source builds).
+#
+# Distros that build via dpkg-buildflags / rpm %optflags already inject
+# these; this block protects operators who do a plain `cmake .. && make`
+# in a fresh checkout. The flags are well-supported on GCC and Clang
+# back to the GR 3.10 / GCC 9 baseline and are no-ops on older
+# toolchains that silently ignore unknown options. -fPIE deliberately
+# omitted: gr-satellites ships as a shared library and PIE objects
+# cannot link into a .so output.
+########################################################################
+if(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
+    add_compile_options(
+        -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=2
+        -fstack-protector-strong)
+    add_link_options(
+        -Wl,-z,relro
+        -Wl,-z,now)
+endif()
+
 SET(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)
 SET(CMAKE_C_STANDARD 11)
 
